The rate parameter $\lambda$ for an exponential distribution is $1/\mu$, so $\lambda = 1/1000$.
The cumulative distribution function (CDF) for $X_i$ is $F_{X_i}(x) = 1 - e^{-\lambda x}$ for $x > 0$.
The probability density function (PDF) for $X_i$ is $f_{X_i}(x) = \lambda e^{-\lambda x}$ for $x > 0$.

